{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789781158,"nonce":"a4N6aaiCXciFIoNVIM4qC3bv114=","title":"a method overridden in another module is called directly on the base","message":"`Output.writeInt32` (haxe/io/Output.hx) calls `writeByte`, which\n`BytesOutput` (another file) overrides. The call bound to\n`Output.writeByte` -- the base body, `throw new NotImplementedException()`\n-- so every `writeInt32/16/UInt16/Double` on a BytesOutput threw\n(printed as \"Uncaught exception: \u003caddress\u003e\"). With the stdlib merge\npreviously replacing that base body by a body-less stub, the same wrong\nbinding trapped instead (Issue5693's CRASH).\n\nMechanism: `build_class_vtables` (mir/helpers/vtables.rs) made a method\nvirtual only when an `override` of it was visible in the module being\nlowered (`override_methods`); a base compiled as a dependency never sees\nits subclasses. And in the subclass's module the imported parent had no\nentries in `class_method_by_name`, so the override found no defining class\nand the subclass built no vtable at all (`PosException.toString`,\n`EnumValueMap.copy/compare` showed the same).\n\nFix: the declaration index (`StaticSigIndex`, fed by every parse and now\nalso by the import loader's discovery parse, before anything lowers)\nrecords `override` declarations; a base seeds a virtual slot for each\nmethod the index says a subclass anywhere overrides; a subclass with an\nimported parent takes the parent's slot layout from the index; slots are\nlaid out in method-name order on both sides so the indices agree.\n\nReproducer: /tmp/probe/vd (pkg/Base.hx, pkg/Derived.hx, rayzor.toml);\nfixture haxe-conformance/regressions/CrossModuleOverride.hx.","files":null}]}